North Branford's new community center, located in the Stanley T. Williams School, officially opened to the public yesterday with a ribbon cutting ceremony. While the center had a soft opening last month and has been open to residents, yesterday marked the completion of a project that the town hopes will become a well-used facility for residents of all ages.

[caption id="attachment_35571" align="alignnone" width="300"]<a href="http://cthousegop.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/10/STW-Ribbon-Cutting-web.jpg"><img class="size-medium wp-image-35571" alt="STW Ribbon Cutting web" src="http://cthousegop.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/10/STW-Ribbon-Cutting-web-300x202.jpg" width="300" height="202" /></a> Community leaders and town officials celebrate the grand opening of the Stanley T. Williams Community Center[/caption]

